==German==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|de|bʰerǵʰ}}
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|burg|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*burgz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰerǵʰ-||fortified elevation}}. Compare Dutch {{term|burcht|lang=nl}}, English {{term|borough|lang=en}}, {{term|-bury|&#8209;bury|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|borg|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bʊʁk/|[bʊʁk]|[bʊɐ̯k]|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/bʊɐ̯ç/|lang=de}} {{a|northern and central Germany; chiefly colloquial}}

